---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does reputation damage last?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "IP reputation: days to weeks of clean behavior. Domain reputation: two to eight weeks of disciplined sending; repeated abuse extends it."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does a new domain start with neutral reputation?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Close to it, but new senders face extra scrutiny: Gmail and Yahoo apply stricter limits to domains without sending history."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can one bad campaign ruin everything?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "One campaign with high complaints does real damage; recovery follows the same recipe (authentication, engagement-only volume, patience)."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do free From addresses (gmail.com) have reputation?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "They use the provider's shared reputation: your ability to build independent domain reputation requires your own domain."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Email Sender Reputation: How It Works"
  description="Email sender reputation explained: IP vs domain reputation, how mailbox providers score you, and the levers that move your score up or down."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Sender Reputation</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Email Sender Reputation: How It Works</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Every sending identity carries a reputation score at each mailbox provider: a rolling judgment built from your volume, complaints, engagement, infrastructure, and authentication history. It is the invisible number that decides whether your campaign lands in the inbox or the junk folder.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Two reputations, two layers</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-ink">IP reputation:</strong> attached to the sending address. Damaged by spam volume from that IP, blocklist hits, and sudden spikes. Shared with other senders on pooled IPs.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">Domain reputation:</strong> attached to your From domain (via DMARC alignment). Survives IP changes, which is why aligned sending on a clean domain recovers faster than raw IP reputation.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What moves the score</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>Direction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Recipients marking spam</td><td class="text-sm text-fail">Strong negative</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Low open/read rates over time</td><td class="text-sm text-warn">Negative drift</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Consistent replies and folder moves to inbox</td><td class="text-sm text-pass">Strong positive</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Blocklist listings</td><td class="text-sm text-fail">Severe negative</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Stable volume + full authentication</td><td class="text-sm text-pass">Positive baseline</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">How to check and repair</h2>
      <p>Google Postmaster Tools shows domain/IP reputation for Gmail traffic (needs <a href="/dmarc/">DMARC</a> live). For broader signals: watch bounce and complaint rates in your ESP, run the <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> weekly, and confirm authentication with the homepage scanner. Repair recipe: fix authentication, cut volume to engaged contacts only, remove complainers, hold steady for two to four weeks while the score rebuilds.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does reputation damage last?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">IP reputation: days to weeks of clean behavior. Domain reputation: two to eight weeks of disciplined sending; repeated abuse extends it.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does a new domain start with neutral reputation?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Close to it, but new senders face extra scrutiny: Gmail and Yahoo apply stricter limits to domains without sending history.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can one bad campaign ruin everything?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">One campaign with high complaints does real damage; recovery follows the same recipe (authentication, engagement-only volume, patience).</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do free From addresses (gmail.com) have reputation?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">They use the provider's shared reputation: your ability to build independent domain reputation requires your own domain.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify my changes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Run the record lookup to confirm live values, then check the propagation checker for worldwide agreement. Both tools run in your browser.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What TTL should I use?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">3600 seconds is the default. Drop to 300 a day before changes so cutover is quick, then restore.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Gmail and Yahoo sender requirements →</a></li><li><a href="/how-to-warm-up-email-server/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">How to warm up →</a></li><li><a href="/email-deliverability/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Email deliverability hub →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
